<title>HONG KONG: Wheelock year profit up 3.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Wheelock year profit up 3.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   125.5	vs  122.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    32.0	 vs  29.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  915.5 gain vs  167.1 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    2,535.5    vs  2,459.2</p>
<p>    Turnover		     5,839.8    vs  2,330.9</p>
<p>    Company name		 Wheelock &amp; Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 18-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   September 29</p>
<p>NOTE - Wheelock is an investment holding company which engages in property investment, retailing, hotel operations and manufacturing.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$320.4 million on disposal of long-term investments, gain of HK$470.9 million on disposal of interest in associated companies, gain of HK$188.3 million on disposal of assets by an associated company and loss of HK$64.1 million from costs relating to the closing down of certain store operations.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 43.5 H.K. cents (including an interim dividend of 11.5 cents) vs 41.0 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
